  "question": "Explain the working principle of a capacitor.",
  "gold_answer": "# Introduction\n\n---\n\n## Definition\n\nA capacitor is an electrical component designed to store potential energy in an electric field by accumulating opposite charges on two closely spaced, insulated conducting plates.\n\n---\n\n## Working Mechanism\n\n* **Charge Separation:** When connected to a voltage source, electrons accumulate on one plate, giving it a negative charge, while electrons leave the opposite plate, leaving it positively charged.\n* **Electric Field Storage:** This charge separation creates a stable electric field between the plates, storing energy even after the voltage source is disconnected.\n\n---\n\n## Formula\n\nThe relationship governing charge storage capacity is:\n\n$$Q = CV$$\n\nFor a basic parallel-plate capacitor layout:\n\n$$C = \\frac{\\varepsilon_0 A}{d}$$\n\nWhere:\n* $Q$ represents the total stored charge magnitude\n* $C$ represents the capacitance value measured in Farads ($\\text{F}$)\n* $V$ represents the applied voltage across the plates\n* $A$ represents the area of overlapping plates\n* $d$ represents the distance separating the plates\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nCapacitors store electrical energy by holding opposite charges on isolated plates, creating an internal electric field with a storage capacity that scales with plate area and proximity.",
  "candidate_response": "<thinking>\nThe user wants me to explain the working principle of a capacitor in an interactive textbook format with structured UI blocks, formula cards, and proper section detection. Let me create a comprehensive response that looks like an interactive textbook rather than markdown notes.\n\nI need to structure this as:\n1. Quick Definition card\n2. Key Concepts card\n3. Formula cards (with explain formula and formula lab buttons)\n4. How it works card\n5. Characteristics card\n6. Applications card\n7. Important Notes card\n\nLet me think about the content:\n\nA capacitor is a passive electronic component that stores electrical energy in an electric field. It consists of two conductive plates separated by a dielectric material.\n\nKey formulas:\n- Q = CV (charge stored)\n- C = εA/d (capacitance)\n- E = ½CV² (energy stored)\n- U = Q²/2C (energy in terms of charge)\n\nLet me structure this properly with React components that look like an interactive textbook.\n\nI'll create a comprehensive React component with:\n- Section cards with icons\n- Formula cards with interactive buttons\n- Responsive tables\n- Color-coded sections\n- Interactive elements\n\nLet me write the full React component.\n</thinking>\n\n```jsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport katex from \"https://esm.sh/katex\";\n\nconst KaTeX = ({ math, display = false }) => {\n  const html = katex.renderToString(math, {\n    throwOnError: false,\n    displayMode: display,\n  });\n  return (\n    <span\n      dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: html }}\n      style={{ fontFamily: \"KaTeX_Main, serif\" }}\n    />\n  );\n};\n\nconst SectionCard = ({ icon, title, accent, children }) => (\n  <div\n    style={{\n      background: \"#ffffff\",\n      border: `1.5px solid ${accent}33`,\n      borderLeft: `4px solid ${accent}`,\n      borderRadius: \"12px\",\n      padding: \"22px 24px\",\n      marginBottom: \"18px\",\n      boxShadow: \"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)\",\n    }}\n  >\n    <div\n      style={{\n        display: \"flex\",\n        alignItems: \"center\",\n        gap: \"10px\",\n        marginBottom: \"14px\",\n      }}\n    >\n      <span style={{ fontSize: \"20px\" }}>{icon}</span>\n      <h2\n        style={{\n          margin: 0,\n          fontSize: \"15px\",\n          fontWeight: \"700\",\n          color: accent,\n          textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n          letterSpacing: \"0.06em\",\n        }}\n      >\n        {title}\n      </h2>\n    </div>\n    <div style={{ color: \"#2d2d2d\", fontSize: \"15px\", lineHeight: \"1.75\" }}>\n      {children}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n);\n\nconst FormulaCard = ({ title, formula, variables, context }) => {\n  const [tab, setTab] = useState(\"formula\");\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        background: \"linear-gradient(135deg, #0f0c29, #302b63, #24243e)\",\n        borderRadius: \"14px\",\n        padding: \"24px\",\n        marginBottom: \"16px\",\n        color: \"#fff\",\n        boxShadow: \"0 4px 20px rgba(48,43,99,0.35)\",\n      }}\n    >\n      <div\n        style={{\n          fontSize: \"11px\",\n          textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n          letterSpacing: \"0.12em\",\n          color: \"#a78bfa\",\n          marginBottom: \"6px\",\n          fontWeight: \"600\",\n        }}\n      >\n        Formula\n      </div>\n      <div\n        style={{ fontSize: \"17px\", fontWeight: \"700\", marginBottom: \"18px\" }}\n      >\n        {title}\n      </div>\n\n      <div\n        style={{\n          display: \"flex\",\n          gap: \"8px\",\n          marginBottom: \"18px\",\n          flexWrap: \"wrap\",\n        }}\n      >\n        {[\"formula\", \"explain\", \"lab\"].map((t) => (\n          <button\n            key={t}\n            onClick={() => setTab(t)}\n            style={{\n              padding: \"6px 16px\",\n              borderRadius: \"20px\",\n              border: \"none\",\n              cursor: \"pointer\",\n              fontSize: \"12px\",\n              fontWeight: \"600\",\n              background: tab === t ? \"#a78bfa\" : \"rgba(255,255,255,0.1)\",\n              color: tab === t ? \"#fff\" : \"#c4b5fd\",\n              transition: \"all 0.2s\",\n            }}\n          >\n            {t === \"formula\"\n              ? \"📐 Formula\"\n              : t === \"explain\"\n              ? \"💡 Explain\"\n              : \"🔬 Lab\"}\n          </button>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n\n      {tab === \"formula\" && (\n        <div\n          style={{\n            background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.08)\",\n            borderRadius: \"10px\",\n            padding: \"20px\",\n            textAlign: \"center\",\n            fontSize: \"22px\",\n          }}\n        >\n          <KaTeX math={formula} display={true} />\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {tab === \"explain\" && (\n        <div\n          style={{\n            background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.06)\",\n            borderRadius: \"10px\",\n            padding: \"18px\",\n          }}\n        >\n          <div\n            style={{\n              fontSize: \"13px\",\n              color: \"#c4b5fd\",\n              marginBottom: \"12px\",\n              fontStyle: \"italic\",\n            }}\n          >\n            {context}\n          </div>\n          <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: \"8px\" }}>\n            {variables.map((v, i) => (\n              <div\n                key={i}\n                style={{\n                  display: \"flex\",\n                  alignItems: \"center\",\n                  gap: \"12px\",\n                  padding: \"8px 12px\",\n                  background: \"rgba(167,139,250,0.1)\",\n                  borderRadius: \"8px\",\n                  fontSize: \"14px\",\n                }}\n              >\n                <span\n                  style={{\n                    minWidth: \"50px\",\n                    color: \"#fbbf24\",\n                    fontWeight: \"700\",\n                  }}\n                >\n                  <KaTeX math={v.symbol} />\n                </span>\n                <span style={{ color: \"#e2e8f0\" }}>\n                  {v.name}{\" \"}\n                  <span style={{ color: \"#94a3b8\", fontSize: \"12px\" }}>\n                    ({v.unit})\n                  </span>\n                </span>\n              </div>\n            ))}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {tab === \"lab\" && (\n        <FormulaLab formula={formula} title={title} variables={variables} />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nconst FormulaLab = ({ title, variables }) => {\n  const labs = {\n    \"Charge Stored — Q = CV\": {\n      inputs: [\n        { key: \"C\", label: \"Capacitance C\", unit: \"F\", default: 0.001 },\n        { key: \"V\", label: \"Voltage V\", unit: \"V\", default: 12 },\n      ],\n      compute: ({ C, V }) => ({ label: \"Charge Q\", value: (C * V).toFixed(6), unit: \"C\" }),\n    },\n    \"Capacitance — C = ε₀A/d\": {\n      inputs: [\n        { key: \"A\", label: \"Plate Area A\", unit: \"m²\", default: 0.01 },\n        { key: \"d\", label: \"Separation d\", unit: \"m\", default: 0.001 },\n        { key: \"er\", label: \"Relative Permittivity εᵣ\", unit: \"\", default: 1 },\n      ],\n      compute: ({ A, d, er }) => ({\n        label: \"Capacitance C\",\n        value: ((8.854e-12 * er * A) / d).toExponential(4),\n        unit: \"F\",\n      }),\n    },\n    \"Energy Stored — E = ½CV²\": {\n      inputs: [\n        { key: \"C\", label: \"Capacitance C\", unit: \"F\", default: 0.001 },\n        { key: \"V\", label: \"Voltage V\", unit: \"V\", default: 12 },\n      ],\n      compute: ({ C, V }) => ({\n        label: \"Energy E\",\n        value: (0.5 * C * V * V).toFixed(6),\n        unit: \"J\",\n      }),\n    },\n  };\n\n  const lab = labs[title];\n  const [vals, setVals] = useState(\n    lab ? Object.fromEntries(lab.inputs.map((i) => [i.key, i.default])) : {}\n  );\n\n  if (!lab)\n    return (\n      <div\n        style={{\n          color: \"#94a3b8\",\n          fontSize: \"13px\",\n          textAlign: \"center\",\n          padding: \"16px\",\n        }}\n      >\n        No interactive lab available for this formula.\n      </div>\n    );\n\n  const result = lab.compute(vals);\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.06)\",\n        borderRadius: \"10px\",\n        padding: \"18px\",\n      }}\n    >\n      <div\n        style={{\n          fontSize: \"12px\",\n          color: \"#a78bfa\",\n          marginBottom: \"14px\",\n          fontWeight: \"600\",\n          textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n          letterSpacing: \"0.08em\",\n        }}\n      >\n        🔬 Interactive Calculator\n      </div>\n      <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: \"10px\" }}>\n        {lab.inputs.map((inp) => (\n          <div key={inp.key}>\n            <label\n              style={{\n                fontSize: \"12px\",\n                color: \"#c4b5fd\",\n                display: \"block\",\n                marginBottom: \"4px\",\n              }}\n            >\n              {inp.label} {inp.unit && `(${inp.unit})`}\n            </label>\n            <input\n              type=\"number\"\n              value={vals[inp.key]}\n              onChange={(e) =>\n                setVals((v) => ({\n                  ...v,\n                  [inp.key]: parseFloat(e.target.value) || 0,\n                }))\n              }\n              style={{\n                width: \"100%\",\n                padding: \"8px 12px\",\n                borderRadius: \"8px\",\n                border: \"1px solid rgba(167,139,250,0.3)\",\n                background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.08)\",\n                color: \"#fff\",\n                fontSize: \"14px\",\n                outline: \"none\",\n                boxSizing: \"border-box\",\n              }}\n            />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n      <div\n        style={{\n          marginTop: \"16px\",\n          padding: \"14px\",\n          background: \"linear-gradient(135deg, #a78bfa22, #818cf822)\",\n          borderRadius: \"10px\",\n          border: \"1px solid #a78bfa44\",\n          textAlign: \"center\",\n        }}\n      >\n        <div style={{ fontSize: \"12px\", color: \"#c4b5fd\", marginBottom: \"4px\" }}>\n          Result\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ fontSize: \"22px\", fontWeight: \"700\", color: \"#fbbf24\" }}>\n          {result.value}{\" \"}\n          <span style={{ fontSize: \"14px\", color: \"#94a3b8\" }}>\n            {result.unit}\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ fontSize: \"12px\", color: \"#94a3b8\", marginTop: \"2px\" }}>\n          {result.label}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nconst StepCard = ({ steps }) => (\n  <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: \"12px\" }}>\n    {steps.map((s, i) => (\n      <div\n        key={i}\n        style={{\n          display: \"flex\",\n          gap: \"14px\",\n          alignItems: \"flex-start\",\n          padding: \"14px 16px\",\n          background: \"#f8faff\",\n          borderRadius: \"10px\",\n          border: \"1px solid #e0e7ff\",\n        }}\n      >\n        <div\n          style={{\n            minWidth: \"30px\",\n            height: \"30px\",\n            borderRadius: \"50%\",\n            background: \"linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6)\",\n            color: \"#fff\",\n            display: \"flex\",\n            alignItems: \"center\",\n            justifyContent: \"center\",\n            fontWeight: \"700\",\n            fontSize: \"13px\",\n            flexShrink: 0,\n          }}\n        >\n          {i + 1}\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div style={{ fontWeight: \"600\", color: \"#1e1b4b\", fontSize: \"14px\" }}>\n            {s.title}\n          </div>\n          <div style={{ color: \"#4b5563\", fontSize: \"14px\", marginTop: \"3px\" }}>\n            {s.desc}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    ))}\n  </div>\n);\n\nconst DataTable = ({ headers, rows, accent }) => (\n  <div\n    style={{\n      overflowX: \"auto\",\n      borderRadius: \"10px\",\n      border: `1px solid ${accent}22`,\n    }}\n  >\n    <table style={{ width: \"100%\", borderCollapse: \"collapse\", fontSize: \"14px\" }}>\n      <thead>\n        <tr style={{ background: `${accent}18` }}>\n          {headers.map((h, i) => (\n            <th\n              key={i}\n              style={{\n                padding: \"12px 16px\",\n                textAlign: \"left\",\n                color: accent,\n                fontWeight: \"700\",\n                fontSize: \"12px\",\n                textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n                letterSpacing: \"0.05em\",\n                borderBottom: `2px solid ${accent}33`,\n              }}\n            >\n              {h}\n            </th>\n          ))}\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        {rows.map((row, i) => (\n          <tr\n            key={i}\n            style={{ background: i % 2 === 0 ? \"#ffffff\" : \"#f9fafb\" }}\n          >\n            {row.map((cell, j) => (\n              <td\n                key={j}\n                style={{\n                  padding: \"11px 16px\",\n                  color: \"#374151\",\n                  borderBottom: \"1px solid #f0f0f0\",\n                  verticalAlign: \"top\",\n                }}\n              >\n                {cell}\n              </td>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n);\n\nconst Tag = ({ label, color }) => (\n  <span\n    style={{\n      display: \"inline-block\",\n      padding: \"3px 10px\",\n      borderRadius: \"12px\",\n      background: `${color}18`,\n      color: color,\n      fontSize: \"12px\",\n      fontWeight: \"600\",\n      marginRight: \"6px\",\n      marginBottom: \"6px\",\n      border: `1px solid ${color}33`,\n    }}\n  >\n    {label}\n  </span>\n);\n\nexport default function CapacitorTutor() {\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        maxWidth: \"780px\",\n        margin: \"0 auto\",\n        padding: \"28px 20px\",\n        fontFamily: \"'Inter', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif\",\n        background: \"#f4f6fb\",\n        minHeight: \"100vh\",\n      }}\n    >\n      {/* Hero Header */}\n      <div\n        style={{\n          background: \"linear-gradient(135deg, #1e3a8a, #3730a3, #4f46e5)\",\n          borderRadius: \"16px\",\n          padding: \"32px 28px\",\n          marginBottom: \"24px\",\n          color: \"#fff\",\n          position: \"relative\",\n          overflow: \"hidden\",\n        }}\n      >\n        <div\n          style={{\n            position: \"absolute\",\n            top: \"-30px\",\n            right: \"-30px\",\n            width: \"160px\",\n            height: \"160px\",\n            borderRadius: \"50%\",\n            background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\",\n          }}\n        />\n        <div\n          style={{\n            fontSize: \"11px\",\n            textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n            letterSpacing: \"0.15em\",\n            color: \"#93c5fd\",\n            marginBottom: \"8px\",\n            fontWeight: \"600\",\n          }}\n        >\n          📘 Physics · Electronics\n        </div>\n        <h1 style={{ margin: \"0 0 10px\", fontSize: \"28px\", fontWeight: \"800\" }}>\n          Capacitor\n        </h1>\n        <p style={{ margin: 0, color: \"#bfdbfe\", fontSize: \"15px\", maxWidth: \"520px\" }}>\n          A passive electronic component that stores electrical energy in an\n          electric field between two conductive plates.\n        </p>\n        <div style={{ marginTop: \"16px\", display: \"flex\", flexWrap: \"wrap\", gap: \"8px\" }}>\n          {[\"Energy Storage\", \"Electric Field\", \"Dielectric\", \"AC Circuits\"].map(\n            (t) => (\n              <span\n                key={t}\n                style={{\n                  padding: \"4px 12px\",\n                  background: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.12)\",\n                  borderRadius: \"20px\",\n                  fontSize: \"12px\",\n                  color: \"#e0f2fe\",\n                  border: \"1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2)\",\n                }}\n              >\n                {t}\n              </span>\n            )\n          )}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      {/* Quick Definition */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"📖\" title=\"Quick Definition\" accent=\"#2563eb\">\n        A <strong>capacitor</strong> is a two-terminal passive component consisting\n        of <strong>two conductive plates</strong> (conductors) separated by an{\" \"}\n        <strong>insulating material</strong> called a <em>dielectric</em>. When\n        connected to a voltage source, it accumulates electric charge on its plates\n        and stores energy in the resulting <strong>electric field</strong>.\n        <div\n          style={{\n            marginTop: \"14px\",\n            padding: \"12px 16px\",\n            background: \"#eff6ff\",\n            borderRadius: \"8px\",\n            border: \"1px solid #bfdbfe\",\n            fontSize: \"14px\",\n            color: \"#1e40af\",\n          }}\n        >\n          💡 Unlike a battery, a capacitor stores energy <em>electrostatically</em>,\n          not chemically — and can release it almost instantaneously.\n        </div>\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Structure */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"🔩\" title=\"Physical Structure\" accent=\"#7c3aed\">\n        <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: \"10px\" }}>\n          {[\n            {\n              part: \"Plate 1 (Conductor)\",\n              desc: \"Positive plate — accumulates positive charge (+Q)\",\n              color: \"#dc2626\",\n            },\n            {\n              part: \"Dielectric\",\n              desc: \"Insulating layer between plates — increases capacitance by reducing effective field\",\n              color: \"#7c3aed\",\n            },\n            {\n              part: \"Plate 2 (Conductor)\",\n              desc: \"Negative plate — accumulates equal negative charge (−Q)\",\n              color: \"#2563eb\",\n            },\n          ].map((item, i) => (\n            <div\n              key={i}\n              style={{\n                display: \"flex\",\n                alignItems: \"center\",\n                gap: \"12px\",\n                padding: \"10px 14px\",\n                background: `${item.color}0d`,\n                borderRadius: \"8px\",\n                border: `1px solid ${item.color}22`,\n              }}\n            >\n              <div\n                style={{\n                  width: \"10px\",\n                  height: \"10px\",\n                  borderRadius: \"50%\",\n                  background: item.color,\n                  flexShrink: 0,\n                }}\n              />\n              <div>\n                <strong style={{ color: item.color, fontSize: \"14px\" }}>\n                  {item.part}\n                </strong>\n                <div style={{ color: \"#4b5563\", fontSize: \"13px\" }}>\n                  {item.desc}\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Working Principle Steps */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"⚙️\" title=\"Working Principle — Step by Step\" accent=\"#059669\">\n        <StepCard\n          steps={[\n            {\n              title: \"Connection to Voltage Source\",\n              desc: \"When a capacitor is connected to a battery or voltage source, an electric potential difference is applied across its two plates.\",\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Charge Accumulation\",\n              desc: \"Electrons flow from the negative terminal of the source onto one plate (making it negative), while electrons are pulled away from the other plate (making it positive).\",\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Electric Field Formation\",\n              desc: \"As charges accumulate, a uniform electric field E develops between the plates, directed from the positive plate to the negative plate.\",\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Dielectric Polarisation\",\n              desc: \"The dielectric material between the plates gets polarised — its molecules align with the field — which weakens the internal field and allows more charge to accumulate.\",\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Equilibrium (Fully Charged)\",\n              desc: \"Charging stops when the voltage across the capacitor equals the source voltage. No steady-state current flows through the dielectric.\",\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Energy Storage\",\n              desc: \"Energy is stored in the electric field between the plates. When the source is removed, this energy remains stored until the capacitor is discharged.\",\n            },\n          ]}\n        />\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Formula 1 */}\n      <FormulaCard\n        title=\"Charge Stored — Q = CV\"\n        formula=\"Q = C \\cdot V\"\n        context=\"The charge stored on a capacitor is directly proportional to the voltage applied across it. This is the fundamental relationship defining capacitance.\"\n        variables={[\n          { symbol: \"Q\", name: \"Charge stored\", unit: \"Coulombs (C)\" },\n          { symbol: \"C\", name: \"Capacitance\", unit: \"Farads (F)\" },\n          { symbol: \"V\", name: \"Voltage across plates\", unit: \"Volts (V)\" },\n        ]}\n      />\n\n      {/* Formula 2 */}\n      <FormulaCard\n        title=\"Capacitance — C = ε₀A/d\"\n        formula=\"C = \\frac{\\varepsilon_0 \\, \\varepsilon_r \\, A}{d}\"\n        context=\"Capacitance depends on the physical geometry of the capacitor and the dielectric material used. A larger plate area and smaller separation increase capacitance.\"\n        variables={[\n          { symbol: \"\\\\varepsilon_0\", name: \"Permittivity of free space\", unit: \"8.854 × 10⁻¹² F/m\" },\n          { symbol: \"\\\\varepsilon_r\", name: \"Relative permittivity (dielectric constant)\", unit: \"dimensionless\" },\n          { symbol: \"A\", name: \"Plate area\", unit: \"m²\" },\n          { symbol: \"d\", name: \"Separation between plates\", unit: \"m\" },\n        ]}\n      />\n\n      {/* Formula 3 */}\n      <FormulaCard\n        title=\"Energy Stored — E = ½CV²\"\n        formula=\"E = \\frac{1}{2} C V^2 = \\frac{Q^2}{2C} = \\frac{QV}{2}\"\n        context=\"The energy stored in a capacitor resides in its electric field. Three equivalent forms exist depending on which quantities are known.\"\n        variables={[\n          { symbol: \"E\", name: \"Energy stored\", unit: \"Joules (J)\" },\n          { symbol: \"C\", name: \"Capacitance\", unit: \"Farads (F)\" },\n          { symbol: \"V\", name: \"Voltage\", unit: \"Volts (V)\" },\n          { symbol: \"Q\", name: \"Charge\", unit: \"Coulombs (C)\" },\n        ]}\n      />\n\n      {/* Types of Capacitors */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"🗂️\" title=\"Types of Capacitors\" accent=\"#d97706\">\n        <DataTable\n          accent=\"#d97706\"\n          headers={[\"Type\", \"Dielectric\", \"Capacitance Range\", \"Best Used For\"]}\n          rows={[\n            [\"Ceramic\", \"Ceramic material\", \"1 pF – 100 µF\", \"High-frequency circuits, decoupling\"],\n            [\"Electrolytic\", \"Aluminium oxide\", \"1 µF – 100,000 µF\", \"Power supply filtering\"],\n            [\"Film (Polyester)\", \"Plastic film\", \"1 nF – 100 µF\", \"Audio, timing circuits\"],\n            [\"Tantalum\", \"Tantalum pentoxide\", \"0.1 µF – 2000 µF\", \"Portable electronics\"],\n            [\"Supercapacitor\", \"Electrolyte layer\", \"1 F – 10,000 F\", \"Energy storage, EVs\"],\n            [\"Mica\", \"Mica mineral\", \"1 pF – 10 nF\", \"RF, precision circuits\"],\n          ]}\n        />\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Charging & Discharging */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"📈\" title=\"Charging & Discharging Behaviour\" accent=\"#0891b2\">\n        <p style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>\n          A capacitor does not charge or discharge instantaneously. The process\n          follows an <strong>exponential curve</strong> governed by the{\" \"}\n          <strong>RC time constant</strong>.\n        </p>\n        <div\n          style={{\n            display: \"grid\",\n            gridTemplateColumns: \"1fr 1fr\",\n            gap: \"12px\",\n            marginTop: \"4px\",\n          }}\n        >\n          {[\n            {\n              label: \"Charging Voltage\",\n              formula: \"V(t) = V_0\\\\left(1 - e^{-t/RC}\\\\right)\",\n              color: \"#059669\",\n            },\n            {\n              label: \"Discharging Voltage\",\n              formula: \"V(t) = V_0 \\\\, e^{-t/RC}\",\n              color: \"#dc2626\",\n            },\n          ].map((item, i) => (\n            <div\n              key={i}\n              style={{\n                padding: \"14px\",\n                background: `${item.color}0d`,\n                borderRadius: \"10px\",\n                border: `1px solid ${item.color}33`,\n                textAlign: \"center\",\n              }}\n            >\n              <div\n                style={{\n                  fontSize: \"12px\",\n                  fontWeight: \"600\",\n                  color: item.color,\n                  marginBottom: \"10px\",\n                }}\n              >\n                {item.label}\n              </div>\n              <KaTeX math={item.formula} display={true} />\n            </div>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n        <div\n          style={{\n            marginTop: \"14px\",\n            padding: \"12px 16px\",\n            background: \"#f0f9ff\",\n            borderRadius: \"8px\",\n            border: \"1px solid #bae6fd\",\n            fontSize: \"14px\",\n          }}\n        >\n          <strong style={{ color: \"#0369a1\" }}>τ = RC</strong> — The{\" \"}\n          <em>time constant</em>. After one time constant, the capacitor reaches{\" \"}\n          <strong>~63.2%</strong> of full charge. After 5τ, it is considered{\" \"}\n          <strong>fully charged (99.3%)</strong>.\n        </div>\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Applications */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"🚀\" title=\"Applications\" accent=\"#7c3aed\">\n        <div\n          style={{\n            display: \"grid\",\n            gridTemplateColumns: \"repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr))\",\n            gap: \"10px\",\n          }}\n        >\n          {[\n            { icon: \"🔋\", title: \"Energy Storage\", desc: \"Flash cameras, UPS systems\" },\n            { icon: \"🎵\", title: \"Audio Filtering\", desc: \"Crossovers, tone controls\" },\n            { icon: \"⚡\", title: \"Power Supply\", desc: \"Smoothing rectified AC to DC\" },\n            { icon: \"📡\", title: \"Tuning Circuits\", desc: \"Radio frequency selection\" },\n            { icon: \"⏱️\", title: \"Timing Circuits\", desc: \"Oscillators, timers (555)\" },\n            { icon: \"🔌\", title: \"Signal Coupling\", desc: \"Blocking DC, passing AC\" },\n            { icon: \"🛡️\", title: \"Noise Filtering\", desc: \"Decoupling in PCBs\" },\n            { icon: \"🚗\", title: \"EVs & Hybrids\", desc: \"Supercapacitors for regen braking\" },\n          ].map((app, i) => (\n            <div\n              key={i}\n              style={{\n                padding: \"14px\",\n                background: \"#faf5ff\",\n                borderRadius: \"10px\",\n                border: \"1px solid #e9d5ff\",\n              }}\n            >\n              <div style={{ fontSize: \"22px\", marginBottom: \"6px\" }}>{app.icon}</div>\n              <div style={{ fontWeight: \"600\", fontSize: \"14px\", color: \"#4c1d95\" }}>\n                {app.title}\n              </div>\n              <div style={{ fontSize: \"12px\", color: \"#6b7280\", marginTop: \"2px\" }}>\n                {app.desc}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Key Properties */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"📊\" title=\"Key Characteristics\" accent=\"#0f766e\">\n        <DataTable\n          accent=\"#0f766e\"\n          headers={[\"Property\", \"In DC Circuit\", \"In AC Circuit\"]}\n          rows={[\n            [\"Current Flow\", \"Only during charging/discharging\", \"Continuous (displacement current)\"],\n            [\"Impedance\", \"Infinite (blocks DC steady state)\", \"Xc = 1/(2πfC) — decreases with frequency\"],\n            [\"Phase Shift\", \"—\", \"Current leads voltage by 90°\"],\n            [\"Energy Loss\", \"None (ideal)\", \"None (ideal); real caps have ESR\"],\n            [\"Behaviour\", \"Open circuit at steady state\", \"Frequency-dependent element\"],\n          ]}\n        />\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Important Notes */}\n      <SectionCard icon=\"⚠️\" title=\"Important Notes\" accent=\"#b45309\">\n        <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: \"10px\" }}>\n          {[\n            {\n              icon: \"⚡\",\n              text: \"Voltage across a capacitor cannot change instantaneously — it requires time to charge or discharge.\",\n            },\n            {\n              icon: \"🔒\",\n              text: \"Electrolytic capacitors are polarised — connecting them in reverse polarity can cause damage or explosion.\",\n            },\n            {\n              icon: \"📐\",\n              text: \"Capacitors in parallel: C_total = C₁ + C₂ + … (capacitances add directly)\",\n            },\n            {\n              icon: \"📐\",\n              text: \"Capacitors in series: 1/C_total = 1/C₁ + 1/C₂ + … (reciprocals add)\",\n            },\n            {\n              icon: \"🌡️\",\n              text: \"Real capacitors have leakage resistance, equivalent series resistance (ESR), and temperature coefficients.\",\n            },\n          ].map((note, i) => (\n            <div\n              key={i}\n              style={{\n                display: \"flex\",\n                gap: \"12px\",\n                padding: \"11px 14px\",\n                background: \"#fffbeb\",\n                borderRadius: \"8px\",\n                border: \"1px solid #fde68a\",\n                fontSize: \"14px\",\n                color: \"#78350f\",\n              }}\n            >\n              <span style={{ flexShrink: 0 }}>{note.icon}</span>\n              <span>{note.text}</span>\n            </div>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </SectionCard>\n\n      {/* Summary */}\n      <div\n        style={{\n          background: \"linear-gradient(135deg, #064e3b, #065f46)\",\n          borderRadius: \"14px\",\n          padding: \"24px\",\n          color: \"#fff\",\n        }}\n      >\n        <div\n          style={{\n            fontSize: \"11px\",\n            textTransform: \"uppercase\",\n            letterSpacing: \"0.12em\",\n            color: \"#6ee7b7\",\n            marginBottom: \"10px\",\n            fontWeight: \"600\",\n          }}\n        >\n          ✅ Summary\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ fontSize: \"15px\", lineHeight: \"1.8\", color: \"#d1fae5\" }}>\n          A capacitor stores energy by separating charge on two conductive plates\n          via an electric field. Its capacitance <KaTeX math=\"C\" /> depends on\n          plate area, separation, and dielectric material. It charges/discharges\n          exponentially with time constant{\" \"}\n          <KaTeX math=\"\\tau = RC\" />, blocks DC in steady state, and acts as a\n          frequency-dependent impedance in AC circuits. Core to filtering, timing,\n          coupling, and energy storage across all of electronics.\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ marginTop: \"16px\", display: \"flex\", flexWrap: \"wrap\" }}>\n          {[\"Q = CV\", \"C = ε₀εᵣA/d\", \"E = ½CV²\", \"τ = RC\", \"Xc = 1/2πfC\"].map(\n            (f) => (\n              <Tag key={f} label={f} color=\"#10b981\" />\n            )\n          )}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```",
